{"t": 1785379912.8, "lenguaje": "html", "temperature": 0.2, "reasoning_effort": null, "max_tokens": null, "system": "You are a creative front-end developer. Write complete, self-contained HTML pages with inline CSS and JavaScript and no external resources. The page must animate by itself on load. Follow the output format exactly.", "prompt": "You are a creative front-end developer making self-contained web pages.\n\nWrite a complete HTML page for: **Un tablero kanban en un solo archivo HTML. OBLIGATORIO: 3 columnas <div class=\"col\"> con data-col todo,doing,done. Las tarjetas son <div class=\"card\"> con data-id. Al cargar hay 3 tarjetas en todo con data-id t1,t2,t3 y las otras columnas vacias. Cada tarjeta tiene <button class=\"mas\"> que la mueve UNA columna a la derecha y <button class=\"menos\"> que la mueve una a la izquierda. Una tarjeta en done no puede avanzar mas; una en todo no puede retroceder. <span id=\"cont-todo\">, <span id=\"cont-doing\"> y <span id=\"cont-done\"> muestran cuantas tarjetas hay en cada columna y se actualizan siempre. REGLA WIP: la columna doing admite COMO MAXIMO 2 tarjetas; si esta llena, el boton mas de las tarjetas de todo no hace nada.. TARGET LOOK, match it: A clean, minimalistic single-page kanban board with three vertical columns labeled “Todo”, “Doing”, “Done”. The hierarchy places the columns side‑by‑side, each with a subtle drop shadow, and the cards stack in a vertical list with soft rounded corners. A muted teal‑blue color palette with white backgrounds and gentle gray accents gives a calm, professional mood. Key elements include the card “mas” (+) and “menos” (−) buttons on each card, and a smooth transition animation when cards move between columns.**\n\nCRITICAL RULES — all must be followed:\n- ONE single self-contained .html file\n- Inline <style> and <script> — no external files\n- NO external resources: no CDN, no <link href=http...>, no fetch(), no remote images or fonts. It must work fully offline.\n- Implement EXACTLY the behavior the idea specifies. Nothing happens on its own: NO setInterval animations and NO random data unless the idea explicitly asks for them.\n- The INITIAL state must match the idea exactly (e.g. a counter that starts at 0 shows 0 and only changes on user action).\n- Reproduce LITERALLY every id=, class= and element the idea marks as required: automated tests will query those exact selectors.\n- Draw charts as inline <svg> — NOT <canvas>, and never a chart library\n- Responsive and legible on a phone screen\n- If you color-code state (up/down, green/red), put the state class on the SAME element your CSS selector targets. A rule like `.row.up span` only works if the class lands on `.row`, not on the inner span.\n- Set colors with a rule that matches the element you actually modify, and prefer setting style/class on the element you create in JS\n- Write ALL visible text in the SAME language as the page topic above\n- If you use <canvas>: set canvas.width = canvas.clientWidth and canvas.height = canvas.clientHeight BEFORE drawing, and redraw on resize. A canvas stretched by CSS from its default 300x150 renders squashed and blurry. Inline <svg> avoids this entirely and is preferred\n- Format numbers for humans: thousands separators, 2 decimals, currency symbol where money (toLocaleString)\n- Render a complete first frame IMMEDIATELY on load — never a blank page waiting for the first setInterval tick\n- REQUIRED component 1: Un tablero kanban en un solo archivo HTML. OBLIGATORIO: 3 columnas <div class=\"col\"> con data-col todo\n- REQUIRED component 2: done. Las tarjetas son <div class=\"card\"> con data-id. Al cargar hay 3 tarjetas en todo con data-id t1\n- REQUIRED component 3: las otras columnas vacias. Cada tarjeta tiene <button class=\"mas\"> que la mueve UNA columna a la derecha y <button class=\"menos\"> que la mueve una a la izquierda. Una tarjeta en done no puede avanzar mas; una en todo no puede retroceder. <span id=\"cont-todo\">\n- REQUIRED component 4: <span id=\"cont-doing\"> y <span id=\"cont-done\"> muestran cuantas tarjetas hay en cada columna\n- REQUIRED component 5: se actualizan siempre. REGLA WIP: la columna doing admite COMO MAXIMO 2 tarjetas; si esta llena\n- REQUIRED component 6: el boton mas de las tarjetas de todo no hace nada.. TARGET LOOK\n- REQUIRED component 7: match it: A clean\n- REQUIRED component 8: minimalistic single-page kanban board with three vertical columns labeled “Todo”\n- REQUIRED component 9: “Done”. The hierarchy places the columns side‑by‑side\n- REQUIRED component 10: each with a subtle drop shadow\n- Implement EVERY required component above — a page that skips any of them is WRONG. Prefer a LONGER page over an incomplete one; there is no size limit.\n- Add configurable constants at the top but no runtime user input.\n\nPROVEN PATTERNS from pages that already passed browser checks and professional review. ADAPT their techniques to this idea — do NOT copy them verbatim; change data, labels, colors and layout to fit:\n--- tabla_estados ---\n<!-- PATRON: tabla de valores con estados pintados sobre los valores VIVOS.\n     Por que funciona: el color va por estilo inline en el MISMO elemento\n     cuyo textContent cambia (no depende de que un selector CSS case);\n     flecha + color, nunca color solo; tabular-nums alinea las columnas. -->\n<table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px\">\n  <thead><tr>\n    <th style=\"text-align:left;color:#898781;font-size:12px\">Valor</th>\n    <th style=\"text-align:right;color:#898781;font-size:12px\">Precio</th>\n    <th style=\"text-align:right;color:#898781;font-size:12px\">Cambio</th>\n  </tr></thead>\n  <tbody id=\"posiciones\"></tbody>\n</table>\n<script>\nfunction fila(sim, precio, cambio) {\n  var tr = document.createElement('tr');\n  var color = cambio >= 0 ? '#006300' : '#d03b3b';\n  var flecha = cambio >= 0 ? '▲' : '▼';\n  tr.innerHTML =\n    '<td><strong>' + sim + '</strong></td>' +\n    '<td style=\"text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums\">' +\n      precio.toLocaleString('es-ES', {style:'currency',currency:'EUR'}) + '</td>' +\n    '<td style=\"text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:' + color + '\">' +\n      flecha + ' ' + Math.abs(cambio).toFixed(2) + '</td>';\n  return tr;\n}\n</script>\n\n\nRespond EXACTLY in this format:\n\nTitle: <short title>\nDescription: <one sentence>\nHTML Code:\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<complete working page>\n```"}
